    "summary": "High‑octane Eleven→Caution suite and fiery Dark Star",
    "blurb": "The show bursts with early‑Feb ’69 energy, highlighted by a scorching The Eleven into Caution jam and a powerful Dark Star that rides the band’s tight interplay. Jerry’s guitar shreds throughout, while the second half maintains momentum despite a muffled Cryptical cut‑off.",
    "review": "On February 5, 1969 at Soldiers' and Sailors' Memorial Hall in Kansas City, KS, the Dead delivered a high‑energy set that still crackles on the solid soundboard capture (gd69-02-05.sbd.cotsman.8993.sbeok.shnf). The first half builds through a tight “Dark Star → Saint Stephen” transition into an electrifying “The Eleven → Caution (Do Not Stop On Tracks)” suite where Jerry Garcia’s shredding is on full display. The band keeps the momentum rolling with a spirited “And We Bid You Good Night”, though the earlier “Cryptical Envelopment” suffers from a muffled mix and an abrupt cut‑off. Overall, despite minor technical hiccups, the performance showcases the group’s early‑’70s improvisational firepower and makes for a compelling listen.",
